module gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cost_debt_straddling_affected_set_universe

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, DeletedWithoutReplacement }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, OutsideTheLadder }

// ITS OWN ROW, NOT A WIDENING OF `floor_cost_debt_straddling_produced_decl`. That row's identity,
// subject and trigger arm (a) -- the produced-decl consumers stop rebuilding the rust TargetModel
// per claim -- are facts about produced-declaration emission witnesses, and this identity is a
// claim-universe witness that never touches a TargetModel. One name over both populations would be
// a section 3 meaning fork, and the widened row's trigger would have an arm that can fire while this
// identity stays withheld, which is the section 4b(3) failure of a trigger naming less than the
// capability it restores. So one row per retirement condition, and this row has exactly one arm.
//
// TYPED, FOR THE SAME REASON THE PRECEDENT ROW IS: the population is one identity, the reason is a
// deletion of coverage with nothing standing in its place on an ordinary floor, and the trigger is a
// capability. `DeletedWithoutReplacement` and not `ReplacementStaged`: the changed-witness override
// (`v2.workflow.required_floor` `changed_witness_cost_policy`) runs this identity for its verdict
// when a change touches it, and is silent for every OTHER change -- a gate added to gunbc.ci_spec,
// a process row dropped from the lens -- that could break the agreement it asserts. Calling that a
// staged replacement would inflate what remains.
//
// THE EVIDENCE, BOTH CLOCKS, IS CARRIED BESIDE THE ROSTER LINE at
// `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt` `floor_cost_debt_straddling_chunk_01` and is not transcribed twice.
// The shape in one line: eval_steps=2884 on every observation, charged CPU 340..568ms at that one
// count, and on one head (gunbc#11173, 26a02cab, run 34730761129) cross, cross, pass with content
// and tree held fixed by construction -- consistent with an environmental contribution to the charge,
// which is the whole of the causal claim; no mechanism is named.
data floor_cost_debt_straddling_affected_set_universe: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "floor_cost_debt_straddling_affected_set_universe" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "one passing claim-universe witness -- the affected-set lens's CI-gate processes joined by identity to the declared gates -- whose charged CPU straddles the required floor's 500ms per-claim ceiling at a constant eval_steps",

  declared: "2026-09-13",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: OutsideTheLadder,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: [
      "v2.test.claim.affected_set_universe.affected_set_universe_gate_processes_match_declared_gates",
    ],
    restoration_trigger: "ONE ARM, A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: the operative required floor ceiling is denominated in CALIBRATED eval_steps, with CPU observed-only, so a claim's cost is qualified on a measure that IS a stable property of the claim rather than on a charge that varies with the claim held fixed -- the capability gunbc.rung_drop floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable is waiting on, and the one that retires it. gunbc#11195 is the lane currently carrying that capability and is cited here as such; the merge of #11195 is NOT the trigger, because a trigger naming less than the capability it restores is satisfied while the capability stays dead. WHAT THIS TRIGGER IS SUFFICIENT FOR, stated because 4b(3) requires it: after it, this identity executes on every ordinary required floor and is decided by a figure that does not change between two runs of one tree -- its 2884 steps, not a charge that moved by up to 67% across observations of those same steps. WHY THIS IS BOUNDED DEBT AND NOT A CLASS REMEDY: the bound is one named identity, one treatment (withheld on ordinary floors, verdict-only under ChangedCostDebtVerdictOnly when touched) and this one retirement condition, not the distance of the carrying lane; the same row shape was refused as a class remedy for gunbc#10994, whose witness carried a real 618,109-step cost, because a row there would have hidden a genuine cost-shape defect, and this identity's eval_steps are constant while its charged CPU varies, with content and tree fixed, in a way consistent with an environmental contribution -- the observations support that and no named mechanism; an earlier draft of this trigger attributed the variation to the runner and was refused as exceeding the evidence. DELETING THE ROSTER LINE FROM v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt, EMPTYING THAT ROSTER, OR SHRINKING THE GATE UNIVERSE THE WITNESS JOINS OVER SATISFIES THE TRIGGER NOT AT ALL -- the first two return the flapping, and the third would shrink the subject to buy the budget.",
  }
}
